The panel-close branch: the inPanel branch checks `line.trim() == '{panel}'` — but the main loop's `_panelOpen.firstMatch(line)` check runs BEFORE the inPanel branch! `{panel}` (the closing tag) MATCHES `_panelOpen` (the `(?::title=…)?` group is optional) → treated as a NEW panel open (no title → emits `>`), staying inPanel.

Fix: the inPanel branch must come BEFORE the panel-open check, or the panel-open check must exclude the bare closing tag. Restructure the main loop:

```dart
if (inPanel) {
  if (line.trim() == '{panel}') { inPanel = false; }
  else out.add('> ${_convertLine(line)}');
  continue;
}
final panel = _panelOpen.firstMatch(line);
if (panel != null) { ... open ... }
```

Move the inPanel check first. The bare `{panel}` closing line when NOT inPanel → stray → skip (the existing `line.trim() == '{panel}'` continue stays after).

