The gates caught my new code — need refactoring (AGENTS.md: "crap4dart is law... design around it rather than fighting it"):

1. **`jiraMarkupToMarkdown` CC=19, 65 lines** — the line-scanner state machine is too complex. Refactor: extract phases into small helpers. Split the loop body:
   - `_convertCodeLine(...)` — inCode branch
   - panel handling → `_convertPanelLine(...)` — needs in/out state... Dart has no ref params; use a small mutable state class.

   Design: a private class `_Converter` holding `inCode`/`inPanel` + output list, with methods per concern:
   ```dart
   class _Converter {
     final _out = <String>[];
     bool _inCode = false, _inPanel = false;
     String convert(String body) {
       for (final line in body.split('\n')) { _line(line); }
       if (_inCode) _out.add('```');
       return _out.join('\n');
     }
     void _line(String line) {
       if (_inCode) { _codeLine(line); return; }
       if (_panelLine(line)) return;
       if (_fencedBlock(line)) return;
       _out.add(_convertLine(line));
     }
     ...
   }
   ```
   Each method small (≤60 lines, CC ≤10). Top-level `jiraMarkupToMarkdown` becomes a 3-line facade.

